erience when you see  people training like this  now this next point is the opposite of  the last one and that's not applying  enough  power into your strikes so there's too  much power and then there's not enough  power remember i spoke about the optimal  balance at the beginning of this video  and a lot of this just comes down to  actually not really trying hard enough  unfortunately  it's natural that if you're not applying  enough power into at least a portion of  the total strikes you execute then your  body isn't going to benefit from the  conditioning that it otherwise would do  if you were doing that  it's something that i've spoken about  countless times in videos on my channel  as well as the bioneer  but really the best way to condition  yourself for an exercise or an activity  is just by doing the activity again and  again and again however with one very  big caveat which is that it needs to be  done with a sufficient level of effort  in which you push yourself regularly  but not constantly remember that balance  otherwise you just remain at the level  you're currently at  i actually think this point is one of  the main reasons that many martial  artists have kind of stagnated  at their current level of skill actually  and that's because they've become  accustomed to training at a certain pace  and then when i train with them they get  tired easily and i'm thinking you know  you're supposed to be a martial artist  why are you not fit enough to do the  activity we're doing  not enough intensity and i wanted to  stay away from using this word in the  previous sections talking about power  because power and intensity are actually  two different things although there is  some crossover in the middle  the way i like to think about intensity  is more kind of like a high level view  or  theme that you carry into all of your  training sessions  now obviously there's many different  ways that you can use the bag and i'm  certainly not saying there's only one  way